1
00:00:10,830 --> 00:00:11,960
Time!

2
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:14,030
All right, Klingons, pencils down.

3
00:00:16,090 --> 00:00:18,090
Okay, I have "pokh."

4
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,760
Have it. Got it.

5
00:00:20,830 --> 00:00:22,030
Yup. Have it. Have it.

6
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:24,360
Have it. Got it. Yup.

7
00:00:24,430 --> 00:00:25,360
I have "chorrr."

8
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:26,260
Got it. Yup.

9
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:27,460
-"Nekhmakh." -Yeah. Yeah.

10
00:00:27,530 --> 00:00:28,890
And "kreplach."

11
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:30,290
Hold on a second. "Kreplach?"

12
00:00:30,290 --> 00:00:31,120
Yeah.

13
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,510
That isn't Klingon; it's Yiddish for meat-filled dumpling.

14
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:37,560
Well, as it turns out, it's also a Klingon word.

15
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:38,990
Really? Define it.

16
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:43,730
"Kreplach": A hearty Klingon... dumpling.

17
00:00:43,790 --> 00:00:45,090
Judge's ruling?

18
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:46,960
Bilurrrbe.

19
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:50,760
Hey, guys, I need to use your TV.

20
00:00:50,830 --> 00:00:51,930
What's wrong with your TV?

21
00:00:51,990 --> 00:00:53,090
I don't know. It just died.

22
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:54,430
I'm getting a bunch of static.

23
00:00:54,490 --> 00:00:55,590
Did you pay your cable bill?

24
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:59,090
Ugh, you sound just like the cable company.

25
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:00,090
All right, so, shh!

26
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:02,860
Tyra Banks is about to kick someone off  America's Next Top Model.

27
00:01:02,930 --> 00:01:04,590
Excuse me, Penny, but we're...

28
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:05,590
No, no, don't tell her.

29
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:06,660
playing Klingon Boggle.

30
00:01:06,730 --> 00:01:08,390
Aw...

31
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:09,760
What do you mean, "Aw"?

32
00:01:09,830 --> 00:01:12,890
Like she didn't know we were nerds?

33
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:14,160
All right, if you must watch,

34
00:01:14,230 --> 00:01:15,690
then mute it with closed captions, please.

35
00:01:15,760 --> 00:01:17,030
Fine.

36
00:01:20,530 --> 00:01:25,090
All right, Boggle warriors... kapla'!

37
00:01:31,430 --> 00:01:34,430
Look at those women.

38
00:01:34,490 --> 00:01:35,760
They're gorgeous.

39
00:01:35,830 --> 00:01:38,830
Oh! "Worf," nice! Too bad that's a proper noun.

40
00:01:40,390 --> 00:01:43,430
Oh, look, the's the future Mrs. Wolowitz.

41
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:46,430
No, wait, that's the future Mrs. Wolowitz.

42
00:01:46,490 --> 00:01:47,830
With her head in the lap of...

43
00:01:47,890 --> 00:01:51,690
Oh, what a coincidence. It's the future Mrs. Wolowitz.

44
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:54,560
Yeah, and they can all move in with you and your mother.

45
00:01:56,930 --> 00:01:59,190
The current Mrs. Wolowitz.

46
00:02:01,390 --> 00:02:05,330
Is "qochbe'" spelled with a (gargling) or a (guttural grunt)?

47
00:02:05,390 --> 00:02:08,990
Why is that Mrs. Wolowitz crying?

48
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:10,160
That's Anais.

49
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:11,430
None of the other girls in the house like her.

50
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:14,390
House? What house?

51
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:16,090
They all live in a house together.

52
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,760
A house, where?

53
00:02:17,830 --> 00:02:19,890
I don't know. Somewhere in L.A.

54
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:23,060
Wait a minute.

55
00:02:26,090 --> 00:02:28,930
You're telling me that I'm within driving distance

56
00:02:28,990 --> 00:02:32,890
of a house filled with aspiring supermodels?

57
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,590
Yeah, I guess.

58
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:40,360
And they live together and shower together and...

59
00:02:40,430 --> 00:02:42,930
have naked pillow fights?

60
00:02:45,430 --> 00:02:46,630
Hey, wh-where are you going?

61
00:02:46,690 --> 00:02:49,590
To pay my cable bill.

62
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:52,890
All right, pencils down!

63
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:57,100
I have "lokh," "makh," and "cherrrkh."

64
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:58,640
Anybody got those?

65
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:33,060
Did I miss anything? Did they kick Giselle off?

66
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:38,000
Not yet, but her underwater photo shoot was an embarrassment.

67
00:03:38,010 --> 00:03:42,460
Sadly, Mrs. Giselle Wolowitz is sensitive to chlorine.

68
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:47,400
Lucky for her I like my fashion models pruny and bug-eyed.

69
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:49,000
Sheldon, the food's here.

70
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:50,200
Ooh, there's the house.

71
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:51,600
Freeze frame, freeze frame.

72
00:03:58,060 --> 00:03:59,260
What are you doing?

73
00:03:59,330 --> 00:04:01,500
Marking the star positions and physical landmarks

74
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:05,100
so we can find the house of the supermodels.

75
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:06,260
Why?

76
00:04:06,330 --> 00:04:07,930
Isn't it obvious?

77
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,060
Every week, they kick out a beautiful girl,

78
00:04:10,130 --> 00:04:13,200
making her feel unwanted and without self-esteem.

79
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:17,930
A.k.a. the future Mrs. Howard Wolowitz.

80
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:20,930
-Is my hamburger medium well? -Yes.

81
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,730
-Dill slices, not sweet? -Yes.

82
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:23,860
-Individual relish packets? -Yes.

83
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:25,360
-Onion rings? -Yes.

84
00:04:25,430 --> 00:04:26,530
-Extra breading? -I asked.

85
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:28,460
-What did they say? -No. -Did you protest?

86
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:30,030
-Yes. -Vociferously? -No.

87
00:04:30,100 --> 00:04:32,330
Well, then what took you so long?

88
00:04:33,330 --> 00:04:34,660
Just eat.

89
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:37,400
Hey, guys, what'd I miss? What'd I miss?

90
00:04:37,460 --> 00:04:39,700
Giselle's hanging by a thread.

91
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:41,960
Oh, good, I hate her.

92
00:04:42,030 --> 00:04:45,700
Then you're not invited to our wedding.

93
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:46,700
Here you go.

94
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:47,860
Thank you.

95
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:49,430
Oh, do we have to suffer through this

96
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:52,130
transparently manipulative pseudo-reality again?

97
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:53,360
Yes.

98
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:55,630
You and I have a standing TV schedule,

99
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:58,230
which is the result of extensive debate and compromise.

100
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:00,630
Any alterations except for breaking news

101
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:03,060
have to be pre-approved at the weekly roommate meeting.

102
00:05:03,130 --> 00:05:05,500
Put it on the agenda.

103
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:07,260
But you have to make a motion to put it on agenda.

104
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:10,100
Oh, I'll make a motion, but you're not going to like it.

105
00:05:12,130 --> 00:05:15,060
Fine. Mock Parliamentary procedure.

106
00:05:15,130 --> 00:05:16,160
At least put it on mute.

107
00:05:16,230 --> 00:05:19,400
Oh, Giselle's not getting kicked off.

108
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:20,960
It's totally going to be Summer.

109
00:05:22,630 --> 00:05:24,660
What?

110
00:05:24,730 --> 00:05:26,630
Sheldon's onion ring. Just put it back!

111
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,330
It's one onion ring.

112
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:29,600
Just put it back before he comes!

113
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:31,130
No, no, no!

114
00:05:31,200 --> 00:05:32,900
No, I don't think that's where it was.

115
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:33,960
Okay, here he comes.  Deny, deny, people.

116
00:05:34,030 --> 00:05:35,060
Wall of silence.

117
00:05:39,730 --> 00:05:41,430
Who touched my...

118
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:43,800
Penny! Penny did it.

119
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:47,260
Why would you do that?

120
00:05:47,330 --> 00:05:48,330
I don't know. I was hungry?

121
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,700
What's the big deal?

122
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:53,260
The big deal is that nobody touches food on my plate.

123
00:05:53,330 --> 00:05:55,130
All right. Look, I didn't know, I'm sorry.

124
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:58,630
Well, I'm sorry, but that is your second strike.

125
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:02,300
What?

126
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,730
You have two strikes.

127
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:06,530
Three strikes and you're out.

128
00:06:07,530 --> 00:06:10,260
It's a sports metaphor.

129
00:06:10,330 --> 00:06:12,130
A sports metaphor?

130
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,030
Yes, baseball.

131
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:17,960
All right, yeah. I-I'll play along.

132
00:06:18,030 --> 00:06:19,100
What was my first strike?

133
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:20,400
March 18th.

134
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:24,060
You violated my rule about forwarding email humor.

135
00:06:24,130 --> 00:06:25,560
I did?

136
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:29,800
The photo of the cat who wants to "has cheezeburger"?

137
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:32,760
Oh, come on. Everybody loves "LOL cats."

138
00:06:32,830 --> 00:06:38,260
They're cute and they can't spell 'cause they're cats.

139
00:06:38,330 --> 00:06:40,330
I trusted you with my email address,

140
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:43,060
and you betrayed that trust by sending me Internet banality:

141
00:06:43,130 --> 00:06:44,400
strike one.

142
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:47,130
Touching my food: strike two.

143
00:06:49,230 --> 00:06:52,260
Don't worry. They only stay on your record for a year.

144
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:57,000
You can get them removed early, but you have to take his class.

145
00:06:59,030 --> 00:07:00,960
Come on, I touched one onion ring.

146
00:07:01,030 --> 00:07:02,360
Yeah, and then you put it back,

147
00:07:02,430 --> 00:07:06,330
compromising the integrity of all the other onion rings.

148
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:09,600
Oh, honey, the buses don't go where you live, do they?

149
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:15,530
Look, Penny, I wish I could be more lenient with you,

150
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:17,560
but since you've become a permanent member of our social group,

151
00:07:17,630 --> 00:07:19,900
I have to hold you to the same standards as everybody else.

152
00:07:21,260 --> 00:07:23,730
Congratulations. You're officially one of us.

153
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:26,360
One of us, one of us.

154
00:07:26,430 --> 00:07:30,030
Well, what a thrill.

155
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:32,200
You're sitting in my spot.

156
00:07:32,260 --> 00:07:34,330
Oh, jeez, you've got to be kidding me.

157
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:35,460
Leonard, she's in my spot.

158
00:07:35,530 --> 00:07:38,630
Yeah, yeah. Uh, see, here's the thing.

159
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:42,630
After you leave, I still have to live with him.

160
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:45,730
I don't care. I'm taking a stand.

161
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:48,530
Metaphorically.

162
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:51,700
All right, that's it. Strike three.

163
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:53,760
Ooh, strike three.

164
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:56,660
I'm banished?

165
00:07:56,730 --> 00:07:59,160
What the hell kind of crap is that?

166
00:07:59,230 --> 00:08:00,900
Listen, don't worry. I'll talk to him.

167
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,260
Yeah, you do that.

168
00:08:02,330 --> 00:08:04,260
Just so I know, would you be open to taking his class?

169
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:11,860
You can do it online!

170
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,840
So based on our triangulation,

171
00:08:14,910 --> 00:08:16,910
we've narrowed down the location of the Top Model house

172
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:19,610
to three square miles in the Hollywood Hills.

173
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:22,780
Or possibly Durham, Noh Carolina.

174
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:24,740
When we find it, you want to go with us?

175
00:08:24,810 --> 00:08:26,710
To do what?

176
00:08:26,780 --> 00:08:29,540
Party with the pretty girls, dude!

177
00:08:29,610 --> 00:08:30,980
Are you insane?

178
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,640
You're not going to party with them.

179
00:08:32,710 --> 00:08:34,440
You're not even going to get anywhere near that place.

180
00:08:34,510 --> 00:08:38,640
That's what they said to Neil Armstrong about the moon.

181
00:08:38,710 --> 00:08:40,640
No one said anything of the kind to Neil Armstrong.

182
00:08:40,710 --> 00:08:43,640
The entire nation dedicated a decade of effort and treasure

183
00:08:43,710 --> 00:08:45,110
to put a man on the moon.

184
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:47,610
Well, my fellow Americans, before this year is out,

185
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:50,640
we will put a Wolowitz on one of America's top models.

186
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:56,140
And a large number of people will believe it never happened.

187
00:08:57,310 --> 00:08:58,980
Okay, let me guess.

188
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:01,980
A quesadilla with soy cheese for the lactose-intolerant Leonard.

189
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:03,380
Thank you.

190
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:04,980
Shrimp Caesar salad with no almonds

191
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:07,740
for the highly allergic kosher-only-on-the-high-holidays Howard.

192
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:11,110
And for our suddenly "back on the Hindu wagon" Raj,

193
00:09:11,180 --> 00:09:12,780
the meatlover's pizza, no meat.

194
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:16,310
Coming right up.

195
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:17,510
Wait. Excuse me.

196
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:19,940
You forgot my barbecue bacon cheeseburger,

197
00:09:20,010 --> 00:09:22,410
barbecue sauce, bacon and cheese on the side.

198
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:24,610
Oh, I didn't tell you?

199
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:27,310
You're banished from the Cheesecake Factory.

200
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:29,710
Why?

201
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:30,940
Well, you have three strikes.

202
00:09:31,910 --> 00:09:33,780
One: coming in. Two: sitting down.

203
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:36,380
And three: I don't like your attitude.

204
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:37,940
You can't do that.

205
00:09:38,010 --> 00:09:40,240
Not only is it a violation of California state law,

206
00:09:40,310 --> 00:09:43,280
it flies directly in the face of Cheesecake Factory policy.

207
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:44,910
Yeah, no, there's a new policy:

208
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:47,210
No shoes, no shirt, no Sheldon.

209
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:51,710
I bet we could sell that sign all over Pasadena.

210
00:09:53,810 --> 00:09:54,710
Penny, can I talk to you for a minute?

211
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:01,280
Well, here's the thing.

212
00:10:01,340 --> 00:10:05,140
Um, I talked to Sheldon and he feels terrible

213
00:10:05,210 --> 00:10:08,980
and he agrees that he was unreasonable and out of line.

214
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:10,580
Really? Well, that's great.

215
00:10:10,640 --> 00:10:13,640
Yeah, so just apologize to him, okay?

216
00:10:13,710 --> 00:10:17,480
What? I'm not going to apologize to that nutcase.

217
00:10:17,540 --> 00:10:18,780
Oh, come on. It's easy.

218
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:21,010
He'll even tell you what to say.

219
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:22,180
Leard, don't you get it?

220
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:24,080
If you guys keep going along with his insanity,

221
00:10:24,140 --> 00:10:25,390
you're just encouraging him.

222
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:29,650
We're not encouraging. It's more like... knuckling under.

223
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:31,820
Look, I like hanging out with you guys,

224
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:34,180
but I'm not going to apologize for something I didn't do.

225
00:10:34,250 --> 00:10:37,550
Well, actually, technically, you did do it.

226
00:10:38,980 --> 00:10:40,980
That's strike one, Leonard.

227
00:10:42,920 --> 00:10:44,650
There you go: quesadilla.

228
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:46,220
Salad.

229
00:10:46,280 --> 00:10:47,820
There's your pizza.

230
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,780
And thanks to Sheldon's heated discussion

231
00:10:49,850 --> 00:10:50,850
with my manager

232
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:52,450
one barbecue bacon cheeseburger,

233
00:10:52,520 --> 00:10:55,180
barbecue sauce, bacon and cheese on the side.

234
00:10:55,250 --> 00:10:56,580
Thank you.

235
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,220
Go ahead. Eat it.

236
00:11:04,530 --> 00:11:06,330
I dare you

237
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:16,540
That's it. There's the house. I foundAmerica's top models!

238
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:18,580
Are you sure?

239
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:19,740
Look, on the roof.

240
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:22,310
Anais and Giselle are sunbathing.

241
00:11:22,380 --> 00:11:24,680
European-style.

242
00:11:25,980 --> 00:11:27,980
You can recognize people on Google Earth?

243
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:29,480
Of course not.

244
00:11:29,540 --> 00:11:33,480
I got a buddy of mine at NORAD to have a spy drone fly over.

245
00:11:33,540 --> 00:11:36,080
NORAD? You're using military aircraft?

246
00:11:36,140 --> 00:11:40,240
It was already targeted to poke around a nuclear reactor in Siberia.

247
00:11:40,310 --> 00:11:42,480
I took it an hour out of its way, tops.

248
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:45,480
Okay, where is he?

249
00:11:45,540 --> 00:11:48,040
Sheldon? I just dropped him off at the comic book store. Why?

250
00:11:48,110 --> 00:11:50,310
Here. Try and go online.

251
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:54,010
Problem with the WiFi? Just try.

252
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:56,040
Greetings, hamburger toucher.

253
00:11:57,710 --> 00:11:59,110
You are probably wondering

254
00:11:59,180 --> 00:12:01,610
why you cannot IM with your little friends

255
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:04,380
about how much you "heart" various things.

256
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:08,140
This recorded message is alerting you

257
00:12:08,210 --> 00:12:09,680
that I am putting an end

258
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:12,080
to your parasitic piggybacking upon our WiFi.

259
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:13,340
If you want to remedy the situation,

260
00:12:13,410 --> 00:12:16,410
you can contact the phone company,

261
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:21,980
set up your own WiFi and pay for it, or you may apologize to me.

262
00:12:24,310 --> 00:12:25,310
Well?

263
00:12:25,380 --> 00:12:27,580
I reiterate: knuckle under.

264
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:29,640
No, no, no, no, no. It is on.

265
00:12:29,710 --> 00:12:32,440
I am gonna introduce your friend to a world of hurt.

266
00:12:32,510 --> 00:12:35,510
Oh, Penny, you don't want to get into it with Sheldon.

267
00:12:35,580 --> 00:12:39,240
The guy is one lab accident away from being a supervillain.

268
00:12:39,310 --> 00:12:41,880
I don't care. I was in junior rodeo.

269
00:12:41,940 --> 00:12:44,940
I can hogtie and castrate him in 60 seconds.

270
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:48,340
No need to neuter the nerd.

271
00:12:48,410 --> 00:12:49,980
I can get you back online.

272
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:52,440
There, see? Problem solved.

273
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:55,580
Voil?

274
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:59,480
SHELDON: Hello, puny insects.

275
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:02,840
As a consequence of your efforts to circumvent my will,

276
00:13:02,910 --> 00:13:06,780
everyone is awarded one additional strike.

277
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:09,780
Thanks a lot, Howard.

278
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:11,240
What are you complaining about?

279
00:13:11,310 --> 00:13:13,710
I'm the one who has to take the class again.

280
00:13:23,610 --> 00:13:25,380
Hello.

281
00:13:25,440 --> 00:13:28,510
Time to do your laundry, huh?

282
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:30,510
It's Saturday night.

283
00:13:30,580 --> 00:13:32,480
Saturday is laundry night.

284
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:34,310
I know.

285
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:37,080
Every Saturday at 8:15.

286
00:13:37,140 --> 00:13:39,380
Easy to anticipate.

287
00:13:41,940 --> 00:13:43,610
What are you implying?

288
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:46,610
I'm implying that you're a creature of habit.

289
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:49,410
And if something were to prevent you from doing your laundry

290
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,980
on Saturday at 8:15,

291
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:53,340
you might find it...

292
00:13:53,410 --> 00:13:55,740
unpleasant.

293
00:14:01,080 --> 00:14:03,180
Knuckle under? My ass.

294
00:14:10,340 --> 00:14:15,040
Oh, no, are all the machines taken?

295
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:18,940
What are you gonna do?

296
00:14:19,010 --> 00:14:21,080
No problem.

297
00:14:21,140 --> 00:14:24,780
I'll just do my laundry another night.

298
00:14:25,910 --> 00:14:26,910
Another night?

299
00:14:26,980 --> 00:14:29,010
Well, I guess you can try,

300
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,740
but deep inside your heart,

301
00:14:30,810 --> 00:14:34,910
you'll know that laundry night is always Saturday night.

302
00:14:39,110 --> 00:14:42,980
Woman, you are playing with forces beyond your ken.

303
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:46,240
Yeah, well, your ken can kiss my Barbie.

304
00:14:51,310 --> 00:14:52,510
Sheldon. Sheldon!

305
00:14:52,580 --> 00:14:54,180
Sheldon.

306
00:14:57,880 --> 00:14:59,940
Yes?

307
00:15:00,010 --> 00:15:01,540
Where are my clothes?

308
00:15:01,610 --> 00:15:05,440
Your clothes? Yes, I left them in the washers

309
00:15:05,510 --> 00:15:08,040
and when I went down to get them, they were gone.

310
00:15:08,110 --> 00:15:08,610
Really?

311
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:12,110
Despite the sign that says "Do not leave laundry unattended"?

312
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:14,080
Sheldon, where are my clothes?

313
00:15:14,140 --> 00:15:18,380
You know, I do recall seeing some female undergarments.

314
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,740
Where was that?

315
00:15:19,810 --> 00:15:21,340
Oh, yes...

316
00:15:21,410 --> 00:15:23,280
Earlier this evening,

317
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:25,280
I happened to gaze out the window

318
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:27,910
and a brassiere caught my eye.

319
00:15:27,980 --> 00:15:30,580
Do those look familiar?

320
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:33,840
How the hell did you get them up on that telephone wire?

321
00:15:33,910 --> 00:15:36,410
When you understand the laws of physics, Penny,

322
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:38,180
anything is possible.

323
00:15:39,740 --> 00:15:43,740
And may I add: mwuh-ha-ha.

324
00:15:43,810 --> 00:15:45,510
Get them down.

325
00:15:45,580 --> 00:15:46,780
Apologize. Never.

326
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,880
Well, then may I suggest you get a very long stick

327
00:15:48,940 --> 00:15:50,310
and play panty pinata.

328
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:54,980
Look, wait, Sheldon, this has gotten out of hand, okay?

329
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:56,340
I've done some stupid things.

330
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:57,640
You've done some stupid things.

331
00:15:57,710 --> 00:16:00,280
How about we just call it even and move on with our lives?

332
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:01,940
I've done no stupid things.

333
00:16:02,010 --> 00:16:03,710
Look, you've got to meet me halfway here.

334
00:16:03,780 --> 00:16:05,280
I am meeting you halfway.

335
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:07,480
I'm willing to concede that you've done stupid things.

336
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:13,080
Hey, you guys are talking again. Good.

337
00:16:15,010 --> 00:16:17,340
What happened?

338
00:16:17,410 --> 00:16:19,980
Leonard, remember when I said it was on?

339
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:22,140
Well, now it's junior rodeo on.

340
00:16:22,210 --> 00:16:26,380
Oh, not junior rodeo.

341
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:28,910
What did you do?

342
00:16:28,980 --> 00:16:30,680
I had no choice, Leonard.

343
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:32,680
She ruined laundry night.

344
00:16:37,110 --> 00:16:39,410
Mwuh-ha-ha.

345
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:52,340
Telephone wires can't electrocute you, can they?

346
00:16:52,410 --> 00:16:55,110
No. Look, this has to stop.

347
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:58,180
Oh, no, no, no. It is just beginning.

348
00:16:58,240 --> 00:17:02,980
All right, I really didn't want to do this, but...

349
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,680
here.

350
00:17:04,740 --> 00:17:06,510
What's this?

351
00:17:06,580 --> 00:17:09,710
Sheldon's Kryptonite.

352
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:14,680
Oh, my God.

353
00:17:14,740 --> 00:17:17,880
He can never know that I gave that to you.

354
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:20,980
Look, I said I wanted to hurt him, but...

355
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:23,340
but this?

356
00:17:23,410 --> 00:17:26,510
It'll shorten the war by five years

357
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:28,840
and save millions of lives.

358
00:17:32,640 --> 00:17:34,540
Oh, pause it. That's it. Confirmed.

359
00:17:34,610 --> 00:17:38,840
We now have the address of the Top Model house.

360
00:17:38,910 --> 00:17:42,380
God bless you, Google Street View registered trademark.

361
00:17:42,440 --> 00:17:45,380
Okay, for the record,

362
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:47,280
what you're doing is really creepy.

363
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:48,940
You know what? If it's "creepy"

364
00:17:49,010 --> 00:17:52,840
to use the Internet, military satellites, and robot aircraft

365
00:17:52,910 --> 00:17:55,140
to find a house full of gorgeous young models

366
00:17:55,210 --> 00:17:57,180
so that I can drop in on them unexpectedly,

367
00:17:57,240 --> 00:17:59,280
then fine, I'm "creepy."

368
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:05,640
Hello.

369
00:18:05,710 --> 00:18:07,880
Oh, hi. Yeah, hold on a second. I'll get him.

370
00:18:07,940 --> 00:18:08,980
Sheldon, it's for you.

371
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:10,840
Who is it? Your mother.

372
00:18:10,910 --> 00:18:12,980
Oh, good.

373
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:15,340
Hi, Mom. How are you?

374
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:18,140
But, Mom...

375
00:18:20,510 --> 00:18:23,610
she keeps sitting in my spot.

376
00:18:23,680 --> 00:18:27,540
And-and she touched my food.

377
00:18:27,610 --> 00:18:31,540
Okay, yes, I took her clothes, but she started it...

378
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:35,140
No, that's not fair.

379
00:18:35,210 --> 00:18:37,710
Why should I have to apologize?

380
00:18:37,780 --> 00:18:40,140
Yeah, I really don't think this is the kind of thing

381
00:18:40,210 --> 00:18:42,180
Jesus concerns himself with.

382
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:44,610
No, you're right.

383
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:47,140
I don't really know what Jesus thinks about.

384
00:18:47,210 --> 00:18:49,840
All right, good-bye.

385
00:18:51,810 --> 00:18:54,410
Did you tell on me?

386
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:55,880
Are you kidding me?

387
00:18:55,940 --> 00:18:57,440
I already have two strikes.

388
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:06,840
Penny. Penny.

389
00:19:06,910 --> 00:19:08,640
Penny.

390
00:19:10,810 --> 00:19:13,710
I am very, very sorry for what I have done.

391
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:14,940
Here's your laundry.

392
00:19:15,010 --> 00:19:16,680
I rescind your strikes

393
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:19,610
and you are no longer banished.

394
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:22,040
Can I sit wherever I want?

395
00:19:25,080 --> 00:19:26,210
Never mind, never mind.

396
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,880
That's, that's not important.

397
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:29,810
Sheldon, this was big of you.

398
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:31,440
Thank you. I really appreciate it.

399
00:19:31,510 --> 00:19:32,680
Thank you.

400
00:19:32,740 --> 00:19:34,180
Good night, Sheldon.

401
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:35,640
Penny...

402
00:19:35,710 --> 00:19:36,880
Yes?

403
00:19:36,940 --> 00:19:38,840
Well played.

404
00:19:41,540 --> 00:19:43,240
Thank you.

405
00:19:43,310 --> 00:19:48,640
Just remember: with great power comes great responsibility.

406
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:51,880
Understood.

407
00:20:07,230 --> 00:20:08,550
Can I help you

408
00:20:09,190 --> 00:20:11,020
Yes, we here to fix the cable.

409
00:20:12,590 --> 00:20:14,860
I think we have satellite.

410
00:20:16,090 --> 00:20:17,740
That's what I meant.

411
00:20:18,450 --> 00:20:20,830
Oh. Okay, come on in.

412
00:20:27,020 --> 00:20:30,750
She's taller than all the women in my family combined.

413
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:33,520
What do we do now?

414
00:20:36,890 --> 00:20:39,080
Follow Mrs. Wolowitz.

